</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:65.6pt;">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Low temperature with repetition</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:131.1pt;">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Repetition is more common at low temperatures and shifts the empirical CDF, which GoF tests exploit effectively.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:10.0pt;padding-right:10.0pt;">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:41.4pt;">
